      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Managed conservation often relies on human control over nature, prioritizing human safety and aesthetics over the complex, chaotic dynamics required for true ecosystem resilience. By suppressing natural processes like fire, invasive species, and mast failure, this outdated model removes the very \"disturbance\" that wild ecosystems need to maintain their health and adapt to change. Viable rewilding requires us to shift from acting *on* the land to acting *with* it, allowing the powerful biological communities to self-regulate and evolve on our own time scale.",
